{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Rise early.</b> It is astonishing: what is the difference that in one place it is written ״בא״ and in another place it is written ״השכם״? And I heard from the Rav Yitzhak z\"l that ״בא״ implies: come with me and I will go with you; but in the other place, where it is written ״השכם,״ it is written ״הנה יוצא המימה״ — meaning, to relieve himself, and it is not the way of honor for the Shekhinah to go there. And it is difficult for me, for even a brief prayer Moses was unwilling to perform in Egypt, because it was full of idols — all the more so the Shekhinah would not go with him. And furthermore, I found that in the warning for the plague of hail it is written ״השכם״ yet it is not written ״הנה יוצא המימה.״ And it appears to me that the matter depends on a new warning: all new warnings were with השכמה, and examine and you will find it so — for with blood you will find written ״לך אל פרעה בבקר,״ since it was the first; and likewise with the warning for דבר, which was new, since the plague before it has no warning — and so too דבר, after which the warning was new, it is therefore written in it ״השכם״; and likewise with hail, which was a new warning, since שחין before it has no warning."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:55.062672816Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}